From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] shermes: retain C layouts and separate exception
 dispatch

Retain bounded string indices, function slots, property-cache ranges,
dense capture slots and shard membership across compatible source edits.
Match serialized literal segments by exact bytes and distinguish ordinary,
typed and non-enumerable shapes. Avoid padding unchanged empty appends.

Emit a separate authenticated layout descriptor, validate and bound each
retained table, and compact excessive retired hints without re-lowering
IR. Layout hints remain optional; current code is always regenerated and
native object reuse still requires exact emitted bytes.

Keep frequently referenced linker bases ahead of changing data pools.
Separate optional setjmp dispatch from instruction bodies while keeping
register and exception state owned by the caller across unwinding.
Apply bounded helper sizes to structural O0 wrappers as well.

Carry emitted manifests, malformed-hint rejection, edit/restore behavior,
typed shapes, capture identity and split-C exception coverage with the
layout and emission implementation.
